{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/750965-2ed-awe-and-lashing-out","id":750965,"title":"[2ed] Awe and Lashing Out","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-03T02:17:44-08:00","id":750965,"title":"[2ed] Awe and Lashing Out","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> When a character use Awe and the npc (or other pc) resist with Lashing Out, do the effect linked with the kind of beast (monstrous, seductive or competitive) used to resist to the power is applied to the PC? Or simply the power doesn't works? <br /> And if the victim of the Awe wins the contested rolls of lashing out, should him be conscious about the use of the awe's attempt by the PC?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T03:30:33-08:00","id":751031,"title":"","content":"Unless you have a merit or power that expressly says it works in conjunction with lashing out (there are some merit chains that augment predatory auras), it doesn't stack. Majesty is called out as not applying to lashing out rolls. If someone successfully lashes out on the majesty user, not only does majesty not work on that individual, but the majesty user is subject to the conditions installed by whomever lashed out.<br /> Yes, because as a former victim of Awe, they're going to notice the awe effects falling off that individual, while everyone else around them is still drooling over the awe user. I tend to have characters' reaction to it kept in context though. Walking into a bar and being hit with the user's awe because he's hunting and didn't know you would be present is not the same as the individual asking to meet with you, then using the effects in order to pile on other effects in order to con you into something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T04:05:24-08:00","id":751079,"title":"","content":"I personally find that the rules on using Lashing Out are a bit odd when it coems to resisting Majesty and Nightmare. Who's the initiator of the struggle, the Majesty user, or the one resisting it? Either way, there's nothing stopping you from using a Seductive Aura with Nightmare, or a Monstrous Aura with Majesty. The Majesty/Nightmare user keeps not only their power active, but inflicts the standard Condition. If the other wins, they're immune to Majesty/Nightmare, and get to inflict a Condition.<br /> <br /> Personally, the way I run things is that the person Lashing Out contests their successes against the Discipline's successes, no further need to test things out on the part of the Discipline user. Too easy to bog down the game with too many dice rolls otherwise, and the systems get confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T05:44:43-08:00","id":751201,"title":"","content":"The Lashing Out isn't a resistance roll. If you successfully Lash Out, it breaks the effect. Not quite the same thing. I find this an important distinction, because Majesty is subtle. You aren't likely to realize you are being affected by Awe right away. It's not a thing you roll to defend yourself, it's a thing you roll when you realize you've been had and want to break out of the effects.<br /> <br /> Aside from this, it functions exactly as any other Lashing Out. Just a side effect of Lashing Out is that it breaks Awe. You don't just go &quot;Okay, X is using Awe, roll Lashing Out to defend yourself.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T06:48:48-08:00","id":751318,"title":"","content":"I confess I'm a little confused about this mechanics <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Cause if Lashing out should be a conscious action to defend himself, this means that awe effect is not so subtle. Otherwise it's not so good to see an elder with hig bp been awed by a child <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T08:06:44-08:00","id":751471,"title":"","content":"I agree with Maina here. Awe and Majesty is so subtle they say right in the description, one doesnt know it's there. So I do not let my players lash out against it unless they have a good reason to believe it's being used against them. For example if this vampire is known for doing it, brags about it, or through observation ( occult or investigation rolls ) <br /> <br /> The initiator of it is the one who chose to lash out and it is most definitely not an automatic roll to resist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:35:42-08:00","id":751693,"title":"","content":"It's covered in the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit?pli=1#heading=h.ryynyiz3rx9v\" target=\"_blank\">FAQ</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does a vampire affected by Majesty 1, Awe, know that they\u2019re being affected by a supernatural power?<br /> Not automatically. They just feel what Awe wants them to feel. However, they retain their faculties enough that if a Daeva seems too amazing to be true, they might be able to turn around and defy it with the predatory aura. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:17:43-08:00","id":751776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/750965-2ed-awe-and-lashing-out?p=751693#post751693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's covered in the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit?pli=1#heading=h.ryynyiz3rx9v&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">FAQ</a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thanks. I lost it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> but now the question is: when is a vampire too much amazing to be true? When he make a exceptional success in the roll while using awe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:44:47-08:00","id":751913,"title":"","content":"It's going to work on a case by case basis, depending on the user of Majesty, those afflicted, and the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T12:00:25-08:00","id":751939,"title":"","content":"I don't use the FAQ answer directly. Instead I let the player decide if their PC wants to lash out or not as soon as the power hits their character. I consider it an instinctual response from the beast, not necessarily the will/logic of the man. I use the 'taking a bane for breaking points' rule where it is clearly states this isn't a conscious decision by the character, but one by the player.<br /> <br /> So far no one's spammed the ability or anything, so it's worked well with my group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}